{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree"],"anchor":"Sorted-sets","title":"Sorted sets","generated":true}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"BinarySearchTrees"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:17BinarySearchTrees5TreapV","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Treap.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap.swift#L31"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Treap"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"Treap"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A sorted set kept in a treap: a binary search tree whose vertices also carry random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"priorities, with no vertex of higher priority than its parent (Seidel and Aragon, 1996).","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Treap"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The random priorities make the shape that of a random binary search tree, whatever order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements arrive in, so lookup, insertion and removal take O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected time. A treap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also splits at an element into the elements below it and the rest, and joins two treaps whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements don’t interleave. The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed by rank like an array: "},{"code":"treap[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"code":["var numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The priorities come from a random number generator given at creation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator"},{"type":"text","text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The treap draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"priorities as its original."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the treap holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/treap"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/Split"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(_:using:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(using:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/height"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/elements(in:)-1pv5t","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/elements(in:)-98uf2","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/join(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/lowerBound(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/max()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/min()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/remove(at:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearch